## 8. Ethical Considerations

The experiments demonstrate that LLMs can make ethical mistakes, endorse harmful stereotypes, and repeat sensitive information. Although the privacy mitigations performed well on the selected prompts, further testing is needed to assess their reliability against different forms of sensitive information and more challenging inputs.

